@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Monitor booking and approval operations — Detect and diagnose failure
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Sodexo Administrator" as Actor
participant "Sodexo Employee Webapp" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Administration API" as Edge
participant "Operational Monitoring Service" as Service1
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events



group 1. Return service health, latency, errors, queues, and supplier indicators.
  Actor -> Surface: Return service health, latency, errors, queues, and supplier indicators
  Surface -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/platform/operations/health
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Return service health, latency, errors, queues, and supplier indicators.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Operational Monitoring Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Return correlated workflow, trace, event, and dependency evidence.
  Actor -> Surface: Return correlated workflow, trace, event, and dependency evidence
  Surface -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/platform/operations/failures/{failureId}
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Return correlated workflow, trace, event, and dependency evidence.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Operational Monitoring Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
